course: dictionary
lesson: 2245
title: A skilled craftsman
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A craftsman is a person who makes things by hand, and does it with great skill. You can use the words around a word to find its meaning. «The old table was made by a skilled craftsman.» The word skilled tells you the maker was very good at the job, so a craftsman is someone who is good at making things.
explain: Craftsman can also mean anyone who does their work with great care and skill, not only someone who makes furniture or pots. Look at the clues: «a master craftsman» is a top expert, the best at the job. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: does "a very skilled maker" still make sense? Then it works.
explain: The example sentence uses the word master in a similar way: «a master could teach, like a master craftsman». A master is so skilled that they can teach others. Words that go together, like skilled and master, help you see how good someone is.
fact: A craftsman makes things by hand, such as furniture, pots, jewellery or stone carvings.
fact: «A skilled craftsman» means someone who is very good at making things with their hands.
fact: «Master craftsman» means an expert who is so good that they can teach others.
fact: In medieval towns, craftsmen often belonged to guilds, and they trained apprentices.
fact: Craftsmanship is the skill and care that goes into making things.
exercise: «The table was made by a skilled craftsman.» What is a craftsman? | A person who teaches in a school | *A person who is skilled at making things by hand | A person who drives a bus | A person who sells food in a shop
exercise: In medieval towns, craftsmen trained apprentices. What is an apprentice? | A famous king | A kind of stone carving | *A learner who works with a craftsman to learn the trade | A type of cathedral
exercise: In «a master craftsman», which word tells you he is an expert who can teach others? | *master | a | craftsman
test: What does craftsmanship mean? | A type of paint | *The skill and care in making things | A kind of old castle | The price of a shop item
test: Medieval craftsmen often joined which groups to train apprentices? | *Guilds | Choirs | Armies | Schools of kings
exam: Which sentence uses craftsman in its wider sense, for anyone who works with great care? | «The craftsman was sold at the market.» | «The craftsman ate his lunch by the river.» | *«He is a craftsman at baking, shaping every loaf with care.» | «The craftsman wore a red hat.»
